7592186045465 13194139533640 true] [17592186243469 1100 "Find the $x$-coordinate of the point on the curve $y={x}^{2}-3x+10$ whose tangent has a slope of $-1.$" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243469 1113 #uuid "55adc6dd-898d-5501-8f26-357be5fee8d8" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243469 1138 false 13194139533640 true] [17592186243469 1145 "Let $f(x)={x}^{2}-3x+10.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-3x+10) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(10) \\\\  & =2x-3\\cdot 1+0 \\\\  & =2x-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set ${f}^{′}(x)=-1$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-3 & =-1 \\\\ 2x & =-1+3 \\\\ 2x & =2 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent is equal to $-1$ at the point where $x=1.$" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243470 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243471 13194139533640 true] [17592186243470 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243472 13194139533640 true] [17592186243470 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243473 13194139533640 true] [17592186243470 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243474 13194139533640 true] [17592186243470 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243475 13194139533640 true] [17592186243470 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533640 true] [17592186243470 1041 "selection" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243470 1104 #edb/ref 17592186243472 13194139533640 true] [17592186243470 1110 #uuid "daa8cdc8-aaf6-5dfe-b5f8-e11b9c15b24c" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243471 1034 "x=-1" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243471 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533640 true] [17592186243471 1111 #uuid "199d38d3-e5b4-5ea3-a948-5c70b563181c" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243472 1034 "x=1" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243472 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533640 true] [17592186243472 1111 #uuid "4e6ffa7e-0fce-55cd-a640-3a03cc6acf82" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243473 1034 "x=2" 