}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=4}=\\frac{7}{2}.\n$$" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243498 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243499 13194139533640 true] [17592186243498 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533640 true] [17592186243498 1041 "field-1" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243498 1104 #edb/ref 17592186243499 13194139533640 true] [17592186243498 1110 #uuid "cb96b9ad-46dd-5b58-9c08-3da5a25e227d" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243499 1034 "\\frac{7}{2}" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243499 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533640 true] [17592186243499 1111 #uuid "a7d1d1cb-00e1-5940-8f1f-750eece037ad" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243500 1017 #edb/ref 17592186243501 13194139533640 true] [17592186243500 1089 "q-342107" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243500 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533640 true] [17592186243500 1100 "Find the exact value of the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y={x}^{6}-4{x}^{4}+8{x}^{2}-4$ at the point where $x=-1.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243500 1113 #uuid "e799e759-0266-55ca-b4f9-da847ab184cf" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243500 1138 false 13194139533640 true] [17592186243500 1145 "Let $f(x)=({x}^{2}-1{)}^{3}+3.$ The slope of the tangent at $x=-1$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(-1).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{d}{dx}\\,({x}^{6}-4{x}^{4}+8{x}^{2}-4) \\\\  & =6{x}^{5}-4(4{x}^{3})+8(2x)-0 \\\\  & =6{x}^{5}-16{x}^{3}+16x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate at $x=-1$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-1) & =6(-1{)}^{5}-16(-1{)}^{3}+16(-1) \\\\  & =-6+16-16 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(-1)=-6.\n$$" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243501 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243502 13194139533640 true] [17592186243501 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243503 13194139533640 true] [17592186243501 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533640 true] [17592186243501 1041 "field-1" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243501 1104 #edb/ref 175