ef 17592186045465 13194139533640 true] [17592186243517 1100 "Find the **positive** $x$-coordinate of the point on the curve $y={x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+14x-6$ whose tangent has a slope of $22.$\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243517 1113 #uuid "33387ec2-9f2b-5805-9498-c0c70b4916a5" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243517 1138 false 13194139533640 true] [17592186243517 1145 "Let $f(x)={x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+14x-6.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+14x-6) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+2x+14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set ${f}^{′}(x)=22$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+2x+14 & =22 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+2x-8 & =0 \\\\ (3x-4)(x+2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-2,\\,\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the positive $x$-coordinate of the points whose tangent has a slope of $6,$ is\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{4}{3}.\n$$" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243518 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243519 13194139533640 true] [17592186243518 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533640 true] [17592186243518 1041 "field-1" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243518 1104 #edb/ref 17592186243519 13194139533640 true] [17592186243518 1110 #uuid "11a57ec6-a9fc-5a80-b71c-39f47076dcc2" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243519 1034 "\\frac{4}{3}" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243519 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533640 true] [17592186243519 1111 #uuid "46f323bc-bde6-5a1f-bcca-a5297b99d0d2" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243520 1017 #edb/ref 17592186243521 13194139533640 true] [17592186243520 1089 "q-48817" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243520 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533640 true] [17592186243520 1100 "Find the $x$-coordinates of the points on the curve $y=-2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+20x-1$ whose tangent has a slope of $2.$" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243520 1113 #uuid "43110fcc-7c49-5c09-8f25-68d9ac38bcdf" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243520 1138 false 13194139533640 true] [17592186243520 1145 "Let $f(x)=-2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+20x-1.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+20x-1) \\\\  & =-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})+6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+20\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 3{x}^{2}+6\\cdot 2x+20\\cdot 1-0 \\\\  & =-6{x}^{2}+12x+20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set ${f}^{′}(x)=2$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{x}^{2}+12x+20 & =2 \\\\ -6{x}^{2}+12x+18 & =0 \\\\ -6({x}^{2}-2x-3) & =0 \\\\ -6(x+1)(x-3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent is equal to $2$ at the points where $x=-1,3.$" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243521 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243522 13194139533640 true] [17592186243521 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243523 13194139533640 true] [17592186243521 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243524 13194139533640 true] [17592186243521 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243525 13194139533640 true] [17592186243521 1000 #edb/ref 17592186243526 13194139533640 true] [17592186243521 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533640 true] [17592186243521 1041 "selection" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243521 1104 #edb/ref 17592186243526 13194139533640 true] [17592186243521 1110 #uuid "b13f85ef-6c81-56b7-b9c8-8f5ad700e1d3" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243522 1034 "x=1" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243522 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533640 true] [17592186243522 1111 #uuid "fb85a957-3069-518f-817d-bcf6a6a1fdc7" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243523 1034 "x=3" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243523 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533640 true] [17592186243523 1111 #uuid "646ed71b-942c-5b68-b1c8-1d35306ba910" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243524 1034 "x=-3" 13194139533640 true] [17592186243524 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533640 true] [17592186243524 1111 #uuid "2fd17713-9b91-50a5-9814-fceceb72ad43" 1